    "title": "Inside Stitch Buffalo: A Vibrant Hub for Textile Arts and Refugee Makers - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Janice Brewster Weiser ,\n1 days ago Stitch Buffalo empowers refugee women through textile arts, offering space, training, and opportunities to create and earn from their craft. When you enter Stitch Buffalo, a community hub in Buffalo, New York’s west side, it’s like walking into a rainbow, says Michelle Perkins, the organization’s development and communications director. “It’s brimming with hope, creativity and lovely, accepting, warm people.” Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 4",
